  "findings": [
    "Formulas and saved input hashes reproduce; the scale L and c on all 30 reserved rows exactly equal the prior baseline.",
    "Training centered correlation has high variance concentration in DA07 and DA08 but is still positive and high when either or both are excluded.",
    "Heldout centered correlation is weak and sensitive to source exclusion; 19/30 order matches in both arms are equal totals, not identical successful pairs.",
    "The shared normalization denominator L can create correlation under some non-geometric predictors, so these behavioral metrics do not establish the model mechanism.",
    "Three reserved variants per source and a posthoc feature diagnostic do not support a claim that all behavior is size memorization.",
    "The centered gold log-ratio variance per row is about 13.5 times larger in training than heldout, so the correlation drop also reflects a narrower heldout dynamic range, not just prediction quality."
  ],
